      "content": "that sounds like a good start. but some of the more technical investors might be pedantic about the p-value thing. if they ask point blank if the results were statistically significant, how should i answer? i don't want to lie and say \"yes\" if we're technically below the 0.05 threshold, but i also can't just say \"no\" or they'll pull the plug on the whole project. what's the best way to handle that specific question?",
